  "generated": "---\ntitle: \"Block numbers\"\nslug: \"/apps/android-blocklist--lg90ce3ygm72r214logejh7k\"\nmdx: {\"format\":\"md\"}\ntags: [\"Android\",\"General\",\"android\",\"blocklist\",\"working-with-contacts\"]\n---\n\n*Looking for an&#x20;*[PC/Mac](/docs/apps/remove-participants-from-a-conference-windows-mac-desktop--nppp2oyqarg76q5ssezwxwp9) *or&#x20;*[iOS](/docs/apps/ios-blocklist--lchl96vtphrmdtytkicr7qo8) *version of this article?*\n\nYou can block incoming calls and SMS from the selected contacts and phone numbers.\n\n**NOTE:**&#x42;locked contacts are shared across your entire organisation, so if you block a number, it will also appear on other users' blocked list.\n\n## How to add a phone number to Block list\n\nTo add a new phone number to your Block list:\n\n1. Navigate to Menu > Blocked.\n2. Tap the \"Add\" button.\n3. On the Create contact screen, specify the phone number and (optionally) the reason for blocking this number.\n4. Press the Save button to confirm.\n\n![](/img/ringotel/original/40a11cdaec9456b6e67a/f330b6b5f8fde61e8c7ceb1d91ddd6766e6ff06118dfe33277119299410813d2.png)\n\n## How to block an existing contact\n\nTo block an existing contact:\n\n1. Navigate to Contacts tab.\n2. Find and select the contact in the list.\n3. In the contact profile, tap on the menu icon and select the Block option.\n\n![](/img/ringotel/original/72fb2013764e4ba8af0a/2756c25747a3e088ac37ab32762c8de9829c2601506811ea3d81dc226d015160.png)\n\n## How to unblock a contact\n\nTo unblock a blocked contact:\n\n1. Navigate to Menu > Blocked.\n2. Find and select the contact in the list.\n3. In the pop-up menu press the \"Remove\" button or open the contact details and unblock in from its profile.\n\n![](/img/ringotel/original/0a3543b8fc3ecb4dff1e/30534b65db612326c2658256b6cca14a8d2878a85f2d49328d00d6397a060e94.png)\n\n## Related articles\n\n- [Create a new contact](/docs/apps/android-create-new-contact--xfi4qswn3bq55vlygnatx1kk)\n- [Working with contacts](/docs/apps/android-working-with-contact--ukprk9ontafcdkvwcit3mzs6)\n"
